concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Appointment of members"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Each member is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument. (2) The Chair and the Deputy Chair must be appointed as full-time members. (3) A member, other than the Chair or the Deputy Chair, may be appointed as a full-time member or as a part-time member. (4) A part-time member may be assigned by the Minister, acting on the ACMA’s advice, on a full-time basis to an inquiry, investigation or hearing. Such an assignment must be in writing. (5) For the purposes of this Act (except for subsection 31(2) and paragraph 34(5)(b)), a part-time member so assigned is taken to be a full-time member while the assignment is in force." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Each member is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument. (2) The Chair and the Deputy Chair must be appointed as full-time members. (3) A member, other than the Chair or the Deputy Chair, may be appointed as a full-time member or as a part-time member. (4) A part-time member may be assigned by the Minister, acting on the ACMA’s advice, on a full-time basis to an inquiry, investigation or hearing. Such an assignment must be in writing. (5) For the purposes of this Act (except for subsection 31(2) and paragraph 34(5)(b)), a part-time member so assigned is taken to be a full-time member while the assignment is in force."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fa626f3e1e15bfb8a74efca72885396121c5615fcc74b6c41747684bc36fd2bb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-20-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-20-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-20-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-20-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-20-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.23" .
doc:sec-20 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20 Appointment of members" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Each member is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument. (2) The Chair and the Deputy Chair must be appointed as full-time members. (3) A member, other than the Chair or the Deputy Chair, may be appointed as a full-time member or as a part-time member. (4) A part-time member may be assigned by the Minister, acting on the ACMA’s advice, on a full-time basis to an inquiry, investigation or hearing. Such an assignment must be in writing. (5) For the purposes of this Act (except for subsection 31(2) and paragraph 34(5)(b)), a part-time member so assigned is taken to be a full-time member while the assignment is in force." ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer .

