concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-22 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "22 Acting Chair"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-22 ;
    values:originalText "The Deputy Chair is to act as the Chair: (a) during a vacancy in the office of Chair (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Chair:   ACMA’s membership  Part 3 Membership  Division 2 Section 23 Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to persons acting as the Chair, see section 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "The Deputy Chair is to act as the Chair: (a) during a vacancy in the office of Chair (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Chair:   ACMA’s membership  Part 3 Membership  Division 2 Section 23 Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to persons acting as the Chair, see section 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "467ed4b73e589e788c63215ebfe67e8672243cc40026a913891106b10458cc8c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Deputy Chair must act as the Chair during a vacancy in the office of Chair or when the Chair is absent from duty or unable to perform duties." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.24" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-22-norm .
