doc:sec-22 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "22 Acting Chair" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The Deputy Chair is to act as the Chair: (a) during a vacancy in the office of Chair (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Chair:   ACMA’s membership  Part 3 Membership  Division 2 Section 23 Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to persons acting as the Chair, see section 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-23 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23 Acting appointments—members other than the Chair"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may appoint a member to act as the Deputy Chair: (a) during a vacancy in the office of Deputy Chair (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Deputy Chair: (i) is acting as the Chair; or (ii) is absent from duty or from Australia; or (iii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. (2) The Minister may appoint a person to act as a member (other than as Chair or Deputy Chair): (a) during a vacancy in the office of a member (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or (b) during any period, or during all periods, when a member: (i) is acting as the Deputy Chair; or (ii) is absent from duty or from Australia; or (iii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may appoint a member to act as the Deputy Chair: (a) during a vacancy in the office of Deputy Chair (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Deputy Chair: (i) is acting as the Chair; or (ii) is absent from duty or from Australia; or (iii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. (2) The Minister may appoint a person to act as a member (other than as Chair or Deputy Chair): (a) during a vacancy in the office of a member (whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office); or (b) during any period, or during all periods, when a member: (i) is acting as the Deputy Chair; or (ii) is absent from duty or from Australia; or (iii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "095c03195357fb8c9461eea59f2b9c25d7319986080f064d5413afa824181b03" ;
    cof:pageNumber "25"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-23-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-23-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.25" .
