doc:sec-25-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "25(3) Period of appointment for associate members" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Despite subsection (1), if:   ACMA’s membership  Part 3 Membership  Division 2 Section 25 Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 (a) an associate member’s instrument of appointment specifies that the appointment relates to a specified inquiry, investigation or hearing; and (b) the inquiry, investigation or hearing ends before the end of the period described in subsection (1); the associate member holds office until the end of the inquiry, investigation or hearing. Extension to complete inquiry, investigation or hearing" ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "25(4) Period of appointment for associate members"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-25-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), if an associate member is conducting, or is part of the panel conducting, an inquiry, investigation or hearing for the ACMA, the Minister may, by writing, extend the associate member’s appointment until the end of the inquiry, investigation or hearing. For 10 year rule, count membership and ABA and ACA membership and associate membership" ;
    skos:definition "(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), if an associate member is conducting, or is part of the panel conducting, an inquiry, investigation or hearing for the ACMA, the Minister may, by writing, extend the associate member’s appointment until the end of the inquiry, investigation or hearing. For 10 year rule, count membership and ABA and ACA membership and associate membership"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cf74ef5bad6fd606035bd5fa0f91f0ff6b2be33577d886012969c0ff3484af0c" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25 ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Extend associate member's appointment until end of inquiry, investigation or hearing." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.26" ;
