doc:sec-38-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "38(2) Presiding at meetings" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the Chair is not present at a meeting, the Deputy Chair presides." ;
    cof:pageNumber "33"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-39 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "39 Quorum"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-39 ;
    values:originalText "(1) At a meeting of the ACMA, a quorum is constituted by a majority of the members. (2) However, if: (a) rules made for the purposes of section 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013 prevent a member from participating in the deliberations, or decisions, of the ACMA with respect to a particular matter; and (b) when the member leaves the meeting concerned there is no longer a quorum present; the remaining members at the meeting constitute a quorum for the purpose of any deliberation or decision at that meeting with respect to that matter." ;
    skos:definition "(1) At a meeting of the ACMA, a quorum is constituted by a majority of the members. (2) However, if: (a) rules made for the purposes of section 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013 prevent a member from participating in the deliberations, or decisions, of the ACMA with respect to a particular matter; and (b) when the member leaves the meeting concerned there is no longer a quorum present; the remaining members at the meeting constitute a quorum for the purpose of any deliberation or decision at that meeting with respect to that matter."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6b582f3f7c9528bfb496db95a04a408e74972f5bf684b25a92815d488b580d81" ;
