concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-41 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41 Voting at meetings etc."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41 ;
    values:originalText "(1) At a meeting of the ACMA, a question is decided by a majority of the votes of the following people present and voting: (a) the members; and   Decision-making and delegation by ACMA  Part 4 Meetings  Division 1 Section 42 Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 (b) if the question relates to a matter connected with an inquiry, investigation, hearing or other matter specified in the instruments of appointment of 1 or more associate members—that associate member, or each of those associate members. (2) The person presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote and, if necessary, also a casting vote." ;
    skos:definition "(1) At a meeting of the ACMA, a question is decided by a majority of the votes of the following people present and voting: (a) the members; and   Decision-making and delegation by ACMA  Part 4 Meetings  Division 1 Section 42 Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 (b) if the question relates to a matter connected with an inquiry, investigation, hearing or other matter specified in the instruments of appointment of 1 or more associate members—that associate member, or each of those associate members. (2) The person presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote and, if necessary, also a casting vote."@en ;
