concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-50 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50 Delegations by ACMA to a Division"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-50 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, delegate to a Division any or all of the ACMA’s functions and powers so far as they relate to the kinds of matters the Division can deal with. (2) A certificate: (a) stating any matter with respect to the performance of a delegated function or exercise of a delegated power; and (b) signed by: (i) a member in the Division; or (ii) an associate member who participated, or could have participated, in the making of the Division’s decision to perform the delegated function or exercise the delegated power; is prima facie evidence of the matter. (3) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in subsection (2) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been duly given unless the contrary is established." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, delegate to a Division any or all of the ACMA’s functions and powers so far as they relate to the kinds of matters the Division can deal with. (2) A certificate: (a) stating any matter with respect to the performance of a delegated function or exercise of a delegated power; and (b) signed by: (i) a member in the Division; or (ii) an associate member who participated, or could have participated, in the making of the Division’s decision to perform the delegated function or exercise the delegated power; is prima facie evidence of the matter. (3) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in subsection (2) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been duly given unless the contrary is established."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "74551a817b92d48015ff011eb7805762d4d6420ffe7fc6b3635d45d1a72c5151" ;
    cof:pageNumber "41"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-50-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-50-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-50-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.41" .
doc:sec-50 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "50 Delegations by ACMA to a Division" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, delegate to a Division any or all of the ACMA’s functions and powers so far as they relate to the kinds of matters the Division can deal with. (2) A certificate: (a) stating any matter with respect to the performance of a delegated function or exercise of a delegated power; and (b) signed by: (i) a member in the Division; or (ii) an associate member who participated, or could have participated, in the making of the Division’s decision to perform the delegated function or exercise the delegated power; is prima facie evidence of the matter. (3) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in subsection (2) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been duly given unless the contrary is established." ;
    cof:pageNumber "41"^^xsd:integer .

