    cml:logicSummary "Division justifies delegation by considering policy and decision requirements." ;
    cml:premiseText "if the delegation is for the purposes of giving effect to a policy or a decision of the Division—having regard to what would be required, necessary or convenient to give effect to the policy or decision," ;
    cml:conclusionText "...the Division is satisfied that it is appropriate for a delegate to exercise the power;" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::argumentation" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-52-ss-1a cml:asserts concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-52-ss-1a-logic-deontic-4 .
concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-52-ss-1a-logic-deontic-4 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Obligation" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Person eligible for delegation must meet specified conditions." ;
    cml:premiseText "the person is: (i) a member; (ii) an SES employee or an acting SES employee; (iii) a person holding, or performing the duties of, an office or position that is at a level equivalent to that of an SES employee." ;
    cml:conclusionText "...if the delegation is for the purposes of giving effect to a policy or decision of the Division—" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-52-ss-1a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "52(1A) Delegations by a Division" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1A) A Division may only delegate a power to make, vary or revoke an instrument that is a legislative instrument to a person under this section if: (a) the delegation is only for the purposes of one or both of the following: (i) giving effect to a policy or a decision of the Division; (ii) making changes of the kinds referred to in each paragraph of subsection 15X(2) of the Legislation Act 2003 (about editorial changes) to instruments made under that power; and (b) if the delegation is for the purposes of giving effect to a policy or a decision of the Division—having regard to what would be required, necessary or convenient to give effect to the policy or decision, the Division is satisfied that it is appropriate for a delegate to exercise the power; and (c) the person is: (i) a member; or (ii) an SES employee or an acting SES employee; or (iii) a person holding, or performing the duties of, an office or position that is at a level equivalent to that of an SES employee. Note: The expressions SES employee and acting SES employee are defined in section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer .

