concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-58 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "58 Advisory committees"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-58 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, establish advisory committees to assist it in performing any of its functions. (2) An advisory committee consists of such persons as the ACMA from time to time appoints to the committee. (3) The ACMA may revoke a person’s appointment to an advisory committee. (4) The ACMA may give an advisory committee written directions as to: (a) the way in which the committee is to carry out its functions; and (b) procedures to be followed in relation to meetings. (5) An appointment to an advisory committee is not a public office within the meaning of the Remuneration Tribunal Act 1973." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, establish advisory committees to assist it in performing any of its functions. (2) An advisory committee consists of such persons as the ACMA from time to time appoints to the committee. (3) The ACMA may revoke a person’s appointment to an advisory committee. (4) The ACMA may give an advisory committee written directions as to: (a) the way in which the committee is to carry out its functions; and (b) procedures to be followed in relation to meetings. (5) An appointment to an advisory committee is not a public office within the meaning of the Remuneration Tribunal Act 1973."@en ;
