concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59C Disclosure to Royal Commissions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-59c ;
    values:originalText "(1) An ACMA official may disclose authorised disclosure information to a Royal Commission (within the meaning of the Royal Commissions Act 1902). (2) The Chair may, by writing, impose conditions to be complied with in relation to authorised disclosure information disclosed under subsection (1). (3) An instrument made under subsection (2) that imposes conditions relating to one particular disclosure identified in the instrument is not a legislative instrument. (4) Otherwise, an instrument made under subsection (2) is a legislative instrument." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An ACMA official may disclose authorised disclosure information to a Royal Commission (within the meaning of the Royal Commissions Act 1902). (2) The Chair may, by writing, impose conditions to be complied with in relation to authorised disclosure information disclosed under subsection (1). (3) An instrument made under subsection (2) that imposes conditions relating to one particular disclosure identified in the instrument is not a legislative instrument. (4) Otherwise, an instrument made under subsection (2) is a legislative instrument."@en ;
