concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59F Disclosure of publicly available information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-59f ;
    values:originalText "(1) An ACMA official may disclose authorised disclosure information if it is already publicly available. (2) For the purposes of this section, an ACMA official is taken to disclose information if the information is published by the ACMA: (a) on the ACMA’s website; or (b) in any other way.   Disclosure of information  Part 7A  Section 59G Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 (3) Subsection (2) is enacted for the avoidance of doubt." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An ACMA official may disclose authorised disclosure information if it is already publicly available. (2) For the purposes of this section, an ACMA official is taken to disclose information if the information is published by the ACMA: (a) on the ACMA’s website; or (b) in any other way.   Disclosure of information  Part 7A  Section 59G Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 (3) Subsection (2) is enacted for the avoidance of doubt."@en ;
