concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59h a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59H Disclosure authorised by regulations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-59h ;
    values:originalText "(1) The regulations may: (a) authorise an ACMA official to disclose authorised disclosure information in specified circumstances; and (b) provide that the Chair may, by writing, impose conditions to be complied with in relation to the disclosure of authorised disclosure information in those circumstances. (2) An instrument made under regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(b) that imposes conditions relating to one particular disclosure identified in the instrument is not a legislative instrument. (3) Otherwise, an instrument made under regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(b) is a legislative instrument. 59J  This Part does not limit disclosure by ACMA official This Part does not limit the circumstances in which an ACMA official is authorised to disclose information." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The regulations may: (a) authorise an ACMA official to disclose authorised disclosure information in specified circumstances; and (b) provide that the Chair may, by writing, impose conditions to be complied with in relation to the disclosure of authorised disclosure information in those circumstances. (2) An instrument made under regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(b) that imposes conditions relating to one particular disclosure identified in the instrument is not a legislative instrument. (3) Otherwise, an instrument made under regulations made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(b) is a legislative instrument. 59J  This Part does not limit disclosure by ACMA official This Part does not limit the circumstances in which an ACMA official is authorised to disclose information."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "29acf80102377fd3aaa391efb6fdcf3f18cb1c30a086c3c8b359583fed229f2c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59h-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59h-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59h-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
