doc:sec-62a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "62A(2) Proceedings in the name of the ACMA" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Proceedings brought against the Commonwealth in relation to the functions or powers of the ACMA may be brought against the Commonwealth in the name of the ACMA.   Other matters  Part 8  Section 62B Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 62B  Decisions relating to the Commonwealth etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "62A(1) Proceedings in the name of the ACMA"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-62a-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The fact that the ACMA does not have a legal identity separate from the Commonwealth does not affect the performance of the ACMA’s functions in making, or the exercise of the ACMA’s powers to make, decisions relating to: (a) the Commonwealth; or (b) any authority of the Commonwealth that is not a body corporate." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The fact that the ACMA does not have a legal identity separate from the Commonwealth does not affect the performance of the ACMA’s functions in making, or the exercise of the ACMA’s powers to make, decisions relating to: (a) the Commonwealth; or (b) any authority of the Commonwealth that is not a body corporate."@en ;
